From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?John=20T=C3=B6rnblom?= <john.tornblom@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:40:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/28] radv/ps4: tessellation's rings where the VGT uses them

Tessellation's VGT registers are the system's on the PS4, as the GS
rings' are, and the orbis-ports mesa-ps4 port measured what RADV's
rings did there:

- VGT_HS_OFFCHIP_PARAM: RADV counts 4 off-chip buffers per CU, 72 here,
  and sizes the off-chip ring for them. Filled with a poison byte, the
  ring's high-water mark over a rendered world was buffer 255, and the
  hardware wrote past the ring: the VGT uses 256 buffers, 8 MiB, which
  is what sceGnmGetOffChipTessellationBufferSize reports.
- VGT_TF_MEMORY_BASE: the VGT reads the factors at the system's factor
  ring, sceGnmGetTheTessellationFactorRingBufferBaseAddress
  (0xff0000000), wherever RADV points the register. Every tessellated
  draw died on a texture-cache read there, where nothing was mapped,
  until memory was mapped at that address and the HS wrote its factors
  to it: then 44 of 44 dEQP-VK.tessellation smoke cases passed.

radeon_info.fixed_tess_factor_ring_va/size give RADV a factor ring of
the system's: the HS's factor ring descriptor points there, the driver's
tessellation rings hold the off-chip ring alone, and VGT_TF_MEMORY_BASE
is written with the address it already holds. The platform maps 2 MiB at
the system's address when it starts, if the address is free, and the
PS4 winsys reports 256 off-chip buffers and an off-chip ring of their
size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Bb93U7uY5qVNuEcHDggEfE
